00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:55.000
The cash that actually lands depends on whether the shares sit in a TFSA, RRSNP, or taxable

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.860
account, because the dividend tax credit applies only in non-registered holdings.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:05.540
The gross-up and credit system can reduce the effective tax rate on eligible Canadian dividends

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:07.600
to 0% in lower brackets.

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:10.540
rates. Most retail investors overlook that

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:15.700
REIT distributions often include return of capital, which lowers the adjusted cost base

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:21.200
and can create larger capital gains later. Check the payout ratio against free cash flow

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:27.480
rather than earnings, because a ratio above 80% on cash flow signals potential cuts even

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:32.420
when earnings appear to cover the dividend. The common misconception is treating every

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:34.340
high yield as sustainable income.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:40.640
Require both a history of dividend growth and a payout ratio below 60% on free cash flow

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:41.800
before adding the name.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:47.100
Dividend growth strategies have historically compounded better than high yield traps in

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:50.540
Canadian non-registered accounts where the tax credit applies.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:56.280
Reads require separate tracking of return of capital portions to avoid unexpected capital

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:58.120
gains tax events years later.

